              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.088,
            0.845,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Using this observation, mentally calculate how much 15% of the values in the table would be."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.141,
            0.801,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose you have to mentally calculate the following percentages of some value: 75%, 90%, 70%, 55%. How would you do it? Discuss."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.134,
            0.904,
            0.19
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.818,
                0.134,
                0.904,
                0.19
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.202,
            0.793,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The FDP Trio — Fractions, Decimals, and Percentages"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.238,
            0.845,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Example 2: We can find 50% of a value by multiplying "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " with the value. Will multiplying the value by 0.5 also give the answer for 50% of the value?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.308,
            0.321,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Yes, since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\textstyle { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } = 0 . 5 ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.711,
            0.308,
            0.843,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "50% of 24 = 12 0.5 × 24 = 12"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.381,
            0.336,
            0.616,
            0.365
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "50\\% = \\frac{50}{100} = \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{0.5}{1} = 0.5."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.369,
            0.845,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Similarly, to find 10% of a quantity, what decimal value should be multiplied?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.424,
            0.441,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Complete the following table:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.461,
            0.839,
            0.585
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.159,
                0.461,
                0.839,
                0.585
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_table_11.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Per cent</td><td>50%</td><td>100%</td><td>25%</td><td>75%</td><td>10%</td><td>1%</td><td>5%</td><td>43%</td></tr><tr><td>Fraction</td><td>50100</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Decimal</td><td>0.5</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.627,
            0.522,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity: How Close Can You Get?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.651,
            0.824,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Make a pair. Each of you choose a number. Suppose, the numbers chosen are a and b. Share your numbers with each other. Both of you should estimate the percentage equivalent to the fraction "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { a } { b }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (where a < b) and announce your answers by a fixed time, say, 5 seconds. The one whose estimate is the closest wins this round. Play this for 10 rounds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.81,
            0.845,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Example 3: The maximum marks in a test are 75. If students score 80% or above in the test, they get an A grade. How much should Zubin score at least to get an A grade?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.873,
            0.847,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can find 80% of 75 in different ways, using our understanding of fraction and decimal multiplication, as well as of proportionality."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.094,
            0.914,
            0.114,
            0.935
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
